/**
 * CODEBASE ENGINEERING
 *
 * Authored from the Memora Smart Technologies curriculum for managing a
 * codebase in AI-assisted software engineering: four phases and ten modules,
 * eight weeks, plus a capstone. The course teaches the work the industry
 * calls program comprehension and codebase ownership: knowing what a project
 * does, what each part is for, what changed and why, and how to change it
 * safely, whether the change is typed by a person or generated by an AI agent.
 *
 * Course content is DATA, never markup, in exactly the shape of the other
 * courses, so the catalog, sidebar, player, progress engine and stats band
 * render it without a change.
 *
 * ── ONE CODEBASE, INVESTIGATED ALL COURSE ────────────────────────────────
 * Every module works on the same unfamiliar project: Kobo Market, a small
 * marketplace with a React frontend, a Node API, sign-in, a cart, Paystack
 * and tests (lib/academy/codebase/). It is built as a real Git repository
 * with a real multi-author history, and every terminal transcript in the
 * lessons is recorded from it by `node scripts/ceRecord.mjs`: Bash in Git
 * Bash, PowerShell, Git, npm, the test runner, ESLint, Vite and the running
 * API. Nothing a lesson shows a command printing was typed by hand.
 *
 * ── THE PRACTICE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Each atom carries one graded practice: a recorded terminal where the
 * learner runs the command that answers a question about the project, a
 * judgement call on a realistic situation, or a JavaScript program whose
 * output they predict (run in Node by `npm run validate:content`). The last
 * lesson of every module is that module's practical assignment.
 *
 * ── THE CURRICULUM TABLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * `curriculum` on each module is the source document's topic list, numbered
 * as it is there (1.1, 1.2, ... with N.P for the practical assignment). Every
 * lesson declares the numbers it `covers`, and `npm run test:academy` fails
 * if any topic is not taught.
 */

